{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Etymology===
''Cease'' essentially meaning "stop", and ''desist'' meaning "do not do it again."

===Verb===
{{infl|en|verb|head=to [[cease]] [[and]] [[desist]]}}

# {{idiomatic|legal}} To stop and to not resume an action. 

====Translations====
* Chinese: [[停止和停止]] (tingzhi huo tingzhi)
* Dutch: [[houd op en doe van afstand]]
* French: [[cessez et renoncez]]
* German: [[hören Sie auf und verzichten Sie]]
* Greek: [[παψτε και σταματήστε]] (papste kai stamatéste)
* Italian: [[cessi e cessi]]
* Japanese: [[終え、止めなさい]] (oe, tomenasai)
* Korean: [[정지하고 단념하십시요]]
* Latin: [[desine et desiste]] {{s}}, desinete et desistete {{p}}
* Spanish: [[cese y renuncia]]

[[Category:English lexical doublets]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[cease]] [[and]] [[desist]]|?}}

# {{legal}} A demanding that one "cease and desist from" continuing certain behavior, such as [[copyright infringement]], [[trademark infringement]], [[slander]], or [[libel]].
#: ''a '''cease-and-desist''' letter''; ''a '''cease-and-desist''' order''

====Usage notes====
*Usually used [[attributive]]ly, as an adjective.